(217, 7, 'Level 19', 'LOOPS AND BRANCHING', 'The Number Grid', 'Pip reaches the final vault, which holds a grid of numbers. The guide searches a two-dimensional array with two nested loops. First comes the setup. A grid is an array of rows, written with double square brackets, int[][], and each row sits in its own pair of braces. Then searchNum holds the value to look for, and foundNum starts as false.

